<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prešov</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Eperjes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prešov is the third-largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a>, in the north-east of the country on the Torysa river. A royal free town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> from the 14th century, it became a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a>, with a Protestant college founded in 1667, and later of Greek Catholic and Rusyn culture. On 16 June 1919 the short-lived Slovak Soviet Republic was proclaimed there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/presov.jpg" alt="Prešov" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ing.Mgr.Jozef Kotulič · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christmas,_Pre%C5%A1ov_21_Slovakia_26.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
